#: ../../source/docs/common-custom-firmware.rst:5
#: 8262b1b479d042018f3404ae50e20d95
msgid "ArduPilot Custom Firmware Builder"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-custom-firmware.rst:7
#: 677cefd74a9b434da3fc50d4ae2b17bc
msgid "As the ArduPilot software evolves through community contributions and development efforts, it’s expanding rapidly with many new features being added. However, not all users need every feature. Depending on their specific requirements and applications, users might prefer to exclude certain features from the software."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-custom-firmware.rst:9
#: 004e4cf3f19d44efa3f772c85ccd0f43
msgid "To address this need, we have developed the **Custom Firmware Builder**, a web application hosted at `custom.ardupilot.org <https://custom.ardupilot.org/>`__. This process helps in reducing the firmware size, making it easier to fit into flight control units (FCUs) with limited flash memory. It also benefits our testers, allowing them to test specific features without needing to upgrade their flight controllers due to space constraints."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-custom-firmware.rst:11
#: 7dec9005c6504d4e8f9a874985eb409b
msgid "The source code of the custom firmware builder can be found `here. <https://github.com/ArduPilot/CustomBuild/>`__"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-custom-firmware.rst:14
#: e7c30866315e48308037a049539a094f
msgid "Submitting a build request"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-custom-firmware.rst:16
#: 994a9f866ffc4241be89f4baab8a091e
msgid "To submit a build request, follow these steps:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-custom-firmware.rst:18
#: 2e0e212311b3442cb5cdf5ca78a71f7c
msgid "Click the **'Add a build'** button located at the top right corner of the homepage."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-custom-firmware.rst:24
#: 7e544d8215c24966a29811563956d3b2
msgid "Choose the vehicle, version, and board,in that order, for which you want to build the firmware."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-custom-firmware.rst:30
#: 4cfdfefe7a8d4093ba41ea6992a23aa5
msgid "Select the features you wish to include in the firmware"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-custom-firmware.rst:32
#: 8714c47577894c32b7601f837f710bb1
msgid "The default features for the board/vehicle will automatically be selected"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-custom-firmware.rst:33
#: c2ad9631ded549ffa249e8e217ec3ef5
msgid "Some features depend on other features so when a feature is selected, all its dependencies will be automatically selected but if the feature is later deselected, the dependencies are not automatically deselected"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-custom-firmware.rst:34
#: 9488e24600e84ec799a425d0c133c723
msgid "It is possible to select a set of features that will not fit on a board which will cause the build will fail."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-custom-firmware.rst:36
#: 8bbf0a87ec0c4ac3981ab5eceb713361
msgid "Click the **'Generate'** button. You will be redirected to the homepage, and a build log for the request you just submitted will appear."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-custom-firmware.rst:37
#: c947462c31e14954b98973fb6b63904c
msgid "Once the build is complete the build artifact will be downloaded automatically, You can also download it manually by clicking the **'Download'** button next to your build request in the build list table. The button will be enabled only after a successful build."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-custom-firmware.rst:38
#: 22946c20cce74f2a9a3652f155afcafa
msgid "Extract the downloaded build artifact. The extracted files will include the .apj firmware file along with other files"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-custom-firmware.rst:39
#: b3a2c61869b94a32a304ac766fc7dc02
msgid "Use your GCS to install the .apj file onto your autopilot.  If using Mission Planner, open the Install Firmware and click then \"Load custom firmware\" link"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-custom-firmware.rst:46
#: 025fb40e0fb34549aebaa218848e94b0
msgid "Versions"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-custom-firmware.rst:49
#: d8accc21efa8414193e4d6aae03626da
msgid "Latest"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-custom-firmware.rst:50
#: 531c7c9a6c8c4740b7bff6a4e4fb04ef
msgid "This is the current development branch of ArduPilot. It includes new features, enhancements, clean-ups, etc. but has not been through a release cycle of beta testing. It has been alpha tested and thoroughly tested in ArduPilot's Continuous Integration auto-test suite. Many experienced users select this to get the latest features but it has the highest risk, in terms of potential bugs."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-custom-firmware.rst:53
#: 97d4cd77878d4dc08ee0970d984daebc
msgid "Beta"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-custom-firmware.rst:54
#: 3d099207484343c0b2471cd9c04c6b44
msgid "This is a release of the development branch used for widespread testing and feedback. While the risk of major issues is low, it is expected that minor behavioral deviations may pop up. These are normally addressed in later beta releases of a major new release before declaring the code as a stable release."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-custom-firmware.rst:57
#: 138f122c5f6f4d389578bf350d94e8c3
msgid "Stable"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-custom-firmware.rst:58
#: 96678fd6fab74113b67cce0b38592044
msgid "These are fully released versions of the code. There are usually several minor releases for each major release number which correct any anomalies found during the beta testing phases. These releases, have the lowest risk. It is recommended that the highest numbered major/minor release be used in a given release sequence, unless an older version is needed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-custom-firmware.rst:61
#: 612df5908d514e12931189fea5c4fd43
msgid "Guide to Size Impacts"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-custom-firmware.rst:63
#: c79a0a57000b4d32a98b4b03599c8912
msgid "Often, the custom build server is used to create firmware with features that have been removed in the standard firmware to conserve flash space, but desired by the user. If a build fails to complete due to lack of flash, the user may remove features/sensors that are  not needed in order to make room for those additional items wanted. In order to facilitate those choices, the table below shows what impact a feature's removal has on flash size. Note that a removed feature in this list automatically removed all features dependent upon it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-custom-firmware.rst:65
#: f782fc77ae4149b59e52814a693fa8ea
msgid "the exact numbers of bytes will change slightly over time due to code changes, but this table should be accurate enough to make decisions on removal candidates to gain flash space."
msgstr ""

